From 4b37833d7aa581a696ba64ea17b8c5498fa88832 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:34:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(desktop): pair session circles with always-on
 linked-card squares [daveey]

Show a 6px linked-card run square immediately after each row's status-dot
lead, outside the fixed lead column, in both flat and card layouts. Keep
non-running card colours in the trailing cluster and ignore blue for its
empty check. Preserve existing status/count derivation and device marks.

The user clarified that idle markers must be grey outlines, not project-tinted.
The shared idle circle now matches the 6px active circle with no fill or
project colour; all non-idle dot variants are unchanged.

Proof: new tests first failed (12 assertions, 106 controls passed); clarified
grey-dot tests failed on the original primitive (3 failures, 22 controls).
GREEN: sidebar plus dot and overlay suites, 81 files / 1101 tests. Full
renderer tsc, applicable eslint, generated desktop keys check and scripts/check
(all 21 checks, including health) pass. No native app relaunch or live bundle
rebuild performed.
